= Why Habits Stick

#epigraph(attribution: [Aristotle, paraphrased])[
  We are what we repeatedly do.
]

Most of what we do each day happens without a decision. We brush our teeth,
take the same route to work and reach for the phone in the same idle moment,
all on autopilot. Researchers estimate that a large share of daily behaviour is
habitual @wood2016.#footnote[The exact share depends on how you count; the
point is that it is large.]

== The habit loop

A habit has three parts: a cue, a routine and a reward. Change any one of
them and the habit weakens.

#pull-quote[You don't rise to the level of your goals. You fall to the level
of your systems.]

#note(title: "Try this")[
  For one week, write down the moment you reach for your phone without
  meaning to. What happened just before?
]

The rest of this chapter looks at each part of the loop in turn.
